From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ip: retain interface flags before releasing the address list
Upstream-Status: Not submitted (downstream-only; upstream writes not authorized)
Source: https://dl.suckless.org/tools/slstatus-1.1.tar.gz
Upstream-License: ISC (see original LICENSE)
Applies-To: slstatus 1.1
Root-Cause: up() dereferenced ifa after freeifaddrs(ifaddr).
Removal-Condition: Drop when an official stable release copies the flags before free.

Preserve the unchanged default datetime configuration and all original objects.
Copy only the required flag before the list is released, retaining original
return values. Mandatory target-only fake-lifetime positive/negative controls
exercise the actual patched and original function; no kernel metric is claimed.

--- a/components/ip.c
+++ b/components/ip.c
@@ -66,5 +66,6 @@ up(const char *interface)
 {
 	struct ifaddrs *ifaddr, *ifa;
+	int is_up;
 
 	if (getifaddrs(&ifaddr) < 0) {
 		warn("getifaddrs:");
@@ -76,7 +77,8 @@ up(const char *interface)
 			continue;
 
 		if (!strcmp(ifa->ifa_name, interface)) {
+			is_up = !!(ifa->ifa_flags & IFF_UP);
 			freeifaddrs(ifaddr);
-			return ifa->ifa_flags & IFF_UP ? "up" : "down";
+			return is_up ? "up" : "down";
 		}
 	}
